# Plan approval under --permission-mode plan: an exit_plan_mode tool
# call raises RenderPlanApproval. Its three options don't support
# arrow-then-commit (permissionview.go: 1/2/3/enter all commit
# immediately at whatever `selected` already is — see
# RenderPlanApproval's doc comment) — this walks the highlight through
# each option, exercises option 3's feedback field, cancels it, then
# commits with option 2 ("manually approve edits").
@faux testdata/faux/qa/permissions-plan-approval.yaml
@args --permission-mode plan

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE plan the rate limiter work
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Ready to code\?/ 20
SHOT plan-option1-highlighted
EXPECT /Here is the plan:/
EXPECT /Yes, and use auto mode/
EXPECT /Yes, manually approve edits/
EXPECT /Tell kiln what to change/
KEY down
SHOT plan-option2-highlighted
KEY down
SHOT plan-option3-highlighted
KEY enter
WAIT 1
SHOT plan-feedback-open
EXPECT /What should change about the plan\?/
TYPE make it use a token bucket instead
SHOT plan-feedback-typed
EXPECT /make it use a token bucket instead/
KEY esc
WAIT 1
SHOT plan-feedback-cancelled
EXPECT_NOT /What should change about the plan\?/
KEY 2
WAITFOR /Plan approved, proceeding/ 20
SHOT plan-approved
EXPECT_NOT /Ready to code\?/
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
